{"text":"All of these feelings that we have are chemically produced feelings. And they're produced by four chemicals, predominantly. These are basically responsible for all of the feelings that I would generically call happiness. They are endorphins, dopamine, serotonin, and oxytocin. Edso. These two chemicals, endorphins and dopamine, I like to call these selfish chemicals, but you don't really need anybody's help to get them. Let me tell you a little bit about what they are. Endorphins. Endorphins are designed to do one thing and one thing only. Mask, physical, pain. That's it. That's what they do. If you're a runner, if you've ever done heavy exercise, you've heard of an endorsement rush or a runner's high. Basically what's happening is when that runner's out there, pushing their bodies harder than they've ever pushed before, they feel good.","words":[{"text":"All","start":0.56,"end":0.86},{"text":"of","start":0.86,"end":1.1},{"text":"these","start":1.1,"end":1.3},{"text":"feelings","start":1.3,"end":1.62},{"text":"that","start":1.62,"end":1.82},{"text":"we","start":1.82,"end":1.96},{"text":"have","start":1.96,"end":2.26},{"text":"are","start":2.26,"end":2.48},{"text":"chemically","start":2.48,"end":2.9},{"text":"produced","start":2.9,"end":3.5},{"text":"feelings","start":3.5,"end":3.98,"punct":"."},{"text":"And","start":4.72,"end":4.98},{"text":"they're","start":4.98,"end":5.18},{"text":"produced","start":5.18,"end":5.5},{"text":"by","start":5.5,"end":6.14},{"text":"four","start":6.14,"end":6.66},{"text":"chemicals","start":6.66,"end":7.4,"punct":","},{"text":"predominantly","start":7.58,"end":7.88,"punct":"."},{"text":"These","start":8.62,"end":8.76},{"text":"are","start":8.76,"end":8.9},{"text":"basically","start":8.9,"end":9.26},{"text":"responsible","start":9.26,"end":9.64},{"text":"for","start":9.64,"end":9.96},{"text":"all","start":9.96,"end":10.16},{"text":"of","start":10.16,"end":10.28},{"text":"the","start":10.28,"end":10.36},{"text":"feelings","start":